<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-001> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> "SR-REQ-001; SR-REQ-019" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-001> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "SR-CPT-001" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-001> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> "CQ-001; CQ-002; CQ-016" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-001> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A context-dependent risk phenomenon or pattern concerning possible effects on value/objectives; distinct from records, descriptions, scores and workflow artifacts."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-001> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk"@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-001> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-013> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-001> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#relatedMatch> <https://purl.org/krdb-core/cover#Risk> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-001> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Paper-1 identity continuity is governed by a stable semantic identity and the #69 identity/continuity contract. Mutable record, assessment, state, ownership and treatment fields do not automatically define or replace Risk identity."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-002> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> "SR-REQ-010" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-002> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "SR-CPT-002" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-002> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> "CQ-013; CQ-017" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-002> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#RoleMixin> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-002> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An entity, value-bearing object or externally owned item about which risk relevance is asserted."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-002> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk Subject"@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-002> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://purl.org/krdb-core/cover#RiskSubject> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-002> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#relatedMatch> <https://purl.org/krdb-core/cover#ObjectAtRisk> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-003> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> "SR-REQ-009" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-003> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "SR-CPT-003" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-003> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> "CQ-012; CQ-028" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-003> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A risk-relevant origin, source or contextual contributor that may participate in a scenario or event; causal status is not implied by the label alone."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk Source"@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-003> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Cross-category contextual/source role pattern. Do not force Risk Source under one gUFO primitive; use typed refinements when the underlying category is known."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-004> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> "SR-REQ-009" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-004> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "SR-CPT-004" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-004> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> "CQ-012; CQ-028" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-004> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A contextual state-of-affairs or situational condition that increases susceptibility to a risk-relevant event/effect without necessarily directly causing it."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Predisposing Condition"@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-004> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#Situation> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-004> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-009> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-004> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Intrinsic disposition-like susceptibility belongs under Vulnerability or an explicit profile refinement; Predisposing Condition remains situational in the Paper-1 Core."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-005> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> "SR-REQ-009" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-005> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "SR-CPT-005" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-005> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> "CQ-012" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-005> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-005> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An occurrence acting as the initiating event for a risk-relevant event or process transition; an enabling condition is represented separately as a Predisposing Condition."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-005> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Trigger"@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-005> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#Event> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-005> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#relatedMatch> <https://purl.org/krdb-core/cover#TriggerEvent> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-006> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> "SR-REQ-002" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-006> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "SR-CPT-006" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-006> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> "CQ-003; CQ-004; CQ-021" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-006> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A risk-relevant situation type specifying a possible configuration, whether or not instantiated; separate from the managed descriptions that express it and from realized events."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk Scenario"@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-006> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#SituationType> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-006> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#Individual> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-006> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-007> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-007> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> "SR-REQ-002; SR-REQ-009" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-007> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "SR-CPT-007" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-007> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> "CQ-003; CQ-012; CQ-021" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-007> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A realized occurrence relevant to a risk context, distinct from a possible scenario and information artifacts describing it."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk Event"@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-007> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#Event> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-007> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://rose.com#RiskEvent> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-007> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://purl.org/krdb-core/cover#RiskEvent> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-008> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> "SR-REQ-009; SR-REQ-013" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-008> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "SR-CPT-008" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-008> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> "CQ-012; CQ-019" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-008> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-008> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A risk-relevant outcome or effect of an event/scenario; its magnitude/severity may be assessed separately."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-008> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Consequence"@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-008> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#Situation> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-008> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-015> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-008> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#relatedMatch> <https://purl.org/krdb-core/cover#ImpactfulOutcome> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-009> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> "SR-REQ-009" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-009> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "SR-CPT-009" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-009> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> "CQ-012" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-009> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A disposition or condition that increases susceptibility to a risk-relevant event/effect."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Vulnerability"@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#IntrinsicMode> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-009> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://rose.com#Vulnerability> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-009> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://purl.org/krdb-core/cover#Vulnerability> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-010> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> "SR-REQ-009; SR-REQ-013" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-010> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "SR-CPT-010" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-010> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> "CQ-012; CQ-019" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-010> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A context-dependent condition or relation indicating how a subject/value is exposed to a risk-relevant source/event; assessment scores remain separate."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Exposure"@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-010> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#Situation> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-011> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> "SR-REQ-003; SR-REQ-012" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-011> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "SR-CPT-011" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-011> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> "CQ-005; CQ-006; CQ-015; CQ-022" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-011> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An activity applying a method, context and evidence to produce one or more risk assessment results."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk Assessment Activity"@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#Event> .
