<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-030> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "SR-CPT-030" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-030> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> "CQ-009; CQ-025" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-030> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#RoleMixin> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-030> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A context-dependent role classification of persons, organizations or other eligible external actors bearing specified risk-management responsibilities; bearer identity is supplied by the external actor kinds, not by ownership."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-030> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk Owner"@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-030> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Paper 1 permits multiple valid responsibility assignments/co-owners and does not impose a unique-owner cardinality; delegation/RACI/committee authority remain profile-level future refinements."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-031> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> "SR-REQ-006" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-031> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "SR-CPT-031" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-031> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> "CQ-009; CQ-025" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-031> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A concrete responsibility/accountability assignment context that depends on an Actor/role bearer and any modeled governance participants, and is about the Risk, artifact, plan or obligation it concerns."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk Responsibility"@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-031> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#Relator> .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-031> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Under the #71 grounding contract, mediation applies to endurant participants; the derived Risk pattern is an aboutness/assignment target rather than a mediated endurant."@en .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-032> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/conformsTo> "SR-REQ-001; SR-REQ-011" .
<urn:semrisk:entity:SR-CPT-032> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "SR-CPT-032" .
